            q: "What is the difference between rekeying and replacing locks?",
            a: "Rekeying changes the internal pin configuration of your existing lock cylinder so old keys no longer work. Lock replacement installs an entirely new lock. Rekeying is significantly less expensive and is the right choice in most situations. Lock replacement makes sense when the hardware is damaged, worn out, or you're upgrading to higher-security locks."
